se the plan had no loop or owner information.\n- Run 2 passed that check and the `#25261` check, then stopped when it created the new While loop. The real loop came with a body containing terminal entries, and the simulator had predicted none.\n\n**Retrospective:** it named two faults, and I accepted both.\n- I wrote the simulator's model of a new loop without first reading what an existing loop's body actually contains.\n- The review gate `guard_peer` blocks work on a log it writes itself (`jev_gate.log`). Two reviews were bought just to get past it.\n\n**Order for cycle 101:** the outcome review issued a steering card saying the next act must be a deliverable build or run, not tool work, and I'm following it. The first card is the display-loop stage itself:\n1. Read the terminal entries of existing loop bodies offline.\n2. Fix the simulator's new-loop model and check it against run 2's real record.\n3. Build the owner map from `D1_s1_copy.vi` itself. Run 2 had used another VI's map as a stand-in, which I rejected.\n4. Re-run the offline checks, then run the stage once, to produce `claudeDev\\D1_s1_disp_<ts>.vi`.\n\nThe `guard_peer` repair follows as a separate card after the stage.\n\nNo new questions for you were added to `decisions_pending.json` this cycle. The runner can continue.","ttft_ms":2046,"type":"result","duration_ms":7847278,"uuid":"774bba13-01cd-4c0a-a559-293997dca804","ttft_stream_ms":1902,"time_to_request_ms":211,"first_content_frame_ms":1902,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
